Here is the root cause:
The buffer size for the firmware command in mlx5_query_nic_vport_mac_list was calculated using the PF's log_max_current_uc/mc_list capabilities, not the queried vport's own capabilities. When a VF vport has a larger configured max (e.g., via devlink), the firmware response can exceed the allocated buffer, causing a slab-out-of-bounds read.

